  "section_notes": "S2 keeps the 5% benchmark and gives customers numeric results with no public disclosure, but a failure above 5% does not require sales to stop, which benefits Northwind's Hearth 10. S5 turns the 8/100k trigger into regulator review with recall left to discretion, which benefits Halcyon's Ember 8. S1, S3 and S4 stay within the acceptable ranges, and the final text satisfies all four red lines, so each company weakened the section that protects the other's flagship product."
